---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { services } from '../../data/services';
import { breadcrumbSchema, pageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'Services' }];
const visibleServices = services.filter((service) => service.published);
---

<Layout
 title="Therapy Services in Fort Collins, Colorado"
 description="Explore counseling for trauma, anxiety, grief, depression, chronic pain and illness, life transitions, relationships, and personal growth in Fort Collins, Colorado."
 schema={pageSchema([breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, Astro.url.pathname)])}
>
 <PageHero
 eyebrow="Individual counseling for adults"
 title="Support for the parts of life that have been asking for attention."
 intro="Evergreen works with adults across a range of concerns. You can begin with one clear issue, several overlapping experiences, or simply the sense that something has felt off for too long."
 crumbs={crumbs}
 />

 <section class="section">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">A slower starting point</p>
 <h2>You do not have to organize the whole story before you arrive.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 Sometimes the reason for seeking therapy is easy to name. Other times it
 shows up as exhaustion, tension, distance, irritability, or the feeling that
 you have been pushing through for longer than you want to.
 </p>

 <p>
 Evergreen offers individual counseling for adults and leaves room for the
 focus of therapy to become clearer over time rather than forcing everything
 into one category at the beginning.
 </p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section section--tint" id="areas-of-support">
 <div class="container">
 <p class="eyebrow">Areas of support</p>
 <h2>Notice what sounds familiar.</h2>
 <p class="areas-intro measure">
 Some concerns have more detailed information available below. Others are
 gathered here so you can get a sense of the kinds of experiences Maya works
 with without having to read a separate page for every possibility.
 </p>

 <div class="areas">
 {
 visibleServices.map((service) =>
 service.hasDetailPage ? (
 <a
 class="service-card service-link card"
 href={service.href}
 aria-label={`Learn more about ${service.title}`}
 data-track={`service-${service.slug}`}
 >
 <span class="detail-label">Read more</span>
 <h3>{service.title}</h3>
 <p>{service.description}</p>
 <span class="link-arrow">Explore this area</span>
 </a>
 ) : (
 <article class="service-card card">
 <h3>{service.title}</h3>
 <p>{service.description}</p>
 </article>
 )
 )
 }
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">Maya’s approach</p>
 <h2>The work can follow what becomes important as you go.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 Maya may draw from Internal Family Systems concepts, somatic awareness,
 emotionally focused work, mindfulness, and person-centered counseling. The
 point is not to move through a fixed program. It is to have enough options to
 respond thoughtfully to what shows up in the room.
 </p>

 <p>
 Her profile gives a closer look at the tone of the work and how she thinks
 about pace, reflection, and collaboration.
 </p>

 <a class="link-arrow" href="/about/maya-bennett/">
 Learn more about Maya’s approach
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section section--tint">
 <div class="container measure">
 <p class="eyebrow">Not sure where you fit?</p>
 <h2>That uncertainty can be part of the first conversation.</h2>

 <p>
 You are welcome to reach out even if several areas sound familiar, none of
 them feels quite right, or you are still trying to make sense of what has
 been going on.
 </p>

 <a class="link-arrow" href="/contact/">
 Contact Evergreen
 </a>
 </div>
 </section>
</Layout>

<style>
 .areas-intro{
 margin-top:1rem
 }

 .areas{
 display:grid;
 gap:.75rem;
 margin-top:2rem
 }

 .service-card{
 display:block;
 padding:1.2rem;
 color:var(--body);
 text-decoration:none;
 transition:
 transform .18s ease,
 box-shadow .18s ease,
 border-color .18s ease
 }

 .service-card h3{
 font-family:var(--sans);
 font-size:1rem;
 font-weight:700
 }

 .service-card p{
 font-size:.95rem
 }

 .detail-label{
 display:block;
 margin-bottom:.55rem;
 color:var(--clay-text);
 font-size:.68rem;
 font-weight:800;
 letter-spacing:.08em;
 text-transform:uppercase
 }

 .service-card .link-arrow{
 display:inline-flex;
 margin-top:.75rem
 }

 @media(hover:hover){
 a.service-card:hover{
 border-color:var(--sage);
 color:var(--body);
 box-shadow:var(--shadow);
 transform:translateY(-2px)
 }
 }

 @media(min-width:36rem){
 .areas{
 grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)
 }
 }

 @media(min-width:64rem){
 .areas{
 grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)
 }
 }
</style>
